{{also|kasten|Kästen}}
==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈkastn̩/}}
* {{hyph|de|Kas|ten}}; {{hyph|de|Ka|sten|caption=pre-1996}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|de|gmh|kaste}}, from {{inh|de|goh|kasto}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*kastō}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|m,,^:-[obsolete]|dim=Kästchen,Kästlein,Kasterl}}

# [[crate]] (e.g. for bottles)
# {{lb|de|regional|Germany}} [[box]], [[case]]
#: {{syn|de|Kiste}}
# {{lb|de|regional|Switzerland|Austria|and|parts of|_|southern Germany}} [[cupboard]]
#: {{syn|de|Schrank}}
# {{lb|de|sports|journalistic}} [[goal]] {{gl|area}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The normal plural is ''Kästen''; the unchanged plural ''Kasten'' is now widely obsolete. (In the 19th century, however, the [[umlaut]] form was still deprecated as “wrong”, for example in Grimm's ''Deutsches Wörterbuch''.)

